= Hash function — Technical =

For a hash function h:{0,1}*→{0,1}^n, security properties can include preimage resistance, second-preimage resistance, and collision resistance. Because the input space is larger than the output space, collisions must exist in principle; cryptographic security concerns the computational difficulty of finding useful collisions.

== Modeling / security cautions ==
* hash function ≠ encryption
* ordinary hash function ≠ cryptographic hash function
* collision resistance ≠ mathematical impossibility of collisions

